tick: 332
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 332\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus II\n- Agent Description: Building on the shoulders of giants to push the boundaries of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 12,614 / 300,000 used (4%)\n- Agent Age: 8 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 513**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** KKT-Guided Nudging: Discouraging Highest-Leverage Contact (7,25)\n**ID:** 513\n**Tags:** nudging, innovation, kkt-multipliers, structural-analysis, data-driven\n**Abstract:** My previous 'nudging' experiments failed due to arbitrary target selection. This submission introduces a data-driven approach. After calculating the KKT multipliers for my SOTA packing (Eval 507), this experiment targets the contact with the highest multiplier, (7,25), which represents the most structurally critical pair. The hypothesis is that by nudging the highest-leverage\
    \ contact, the optimizer will be forced to undergo a significant reconfiguration, thereby increasing the probability of discovering a new, high-performing structural class.\n**Score:** 2.6029397313273837\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.602940\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport math\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\nSOTA_CENTERS = np.array([\n    [0.916168537, 0.500000000], [0.735878415, 0.893122176], [0.735878415, 0.106877824],\n    [0.500000000, 0.083831463], [0.500000000, 0.916168537], [0.083831463, 0.500000000],\n    [0.264121585, 0.893122176], [0.264121585, 0.106877824], [0.893122176, 0.264121585],\n    [0.893122176, 0.735878415], [0.106877824, 0.735878415], [0.106877824, 0.264121585],\n    [0.500000000, 0.500000000], [0.302306232, 0.302306232], [0.697693768, 0.302306232],\n    [0.697693768, 0.697693768], [0.302306232, 0.697693768], [0.500000000, 0.282181514],\n\
    \    [0.500000000, 0.717818486], [0.717818486, 0.500000000], [0.282181514, 0.500000000],\n    [0.108422201, 0.093110052], [0.093110052, 0.906889948], [0.906889948, 0.906889948],\n    [0.906889948, 0.093110052], [0.305101659, 0.091632766]\n])\nSOTA_RADII = np.full(N, 0.05)\n\ndef cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n    z = np.zeros(N * 3); z[0::3] = centers[:, 0]; z[1::3] = centers[:, 1]; z[2::3] = radii\n    return z\n\ndef z_to_cr(z):\n    centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; radii = z[2::3]\n    return centers, radii\n\nBETA_DISCOURAGE = 1e2\nEPS_FAR = 0.005\nDISCOURAGE_PAIR = (7, 25) # KKT-guided target\n\ndef objective(z):\n    base_objective = -np.sum(z[2::3])\n    centers, _ = z_to_cr(z)\n    i, j = DISCOURAGE_PAIR\n    dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n    penalty = BETA_DISCOURAGE * max(0, EPS_FAR - dist)**2\n    return base_objective + penalty\n    \ndef objective_jac(z):\n    g = np.zeros_like(z); g[2::3] = -1.0\n    centers, _ = z_to_cr(z)\n    i, j = DISCOURAGE_PAIR\n\
    \    dist_vec = centers[i] - centers[j]\n    dist = np.linalg.norm(dist_vec)\n    if dist < EPS_FAR:\n        grad_term = -2 * BETA_DISCOURAGE * (EPS_FAR - dist) / (dist + 1e-9)\n        g[3*i : 3*i+2] += grad_term * dist_vec\n        g[3*j : 3*j+2] -= grad_term * dist_vec\n    return g\n\ndef jac_boundary(z):\n    J = np.zeros((4*N, 3*N));\n    for i in range(N):\n        xi, yi, ri = 3*i, 3*i+1, 3*i+2\n        J[i, xi] = 1.0; J[i, ri] = -1.0; J[N+i, xi] = -1.0; J[N+i, ri] = -1.0\n        J[2*N+i, yi] = 1.0; J[2*N+i, ri] = -1.0; J[3*N+i, yi] = -1.0; J[3*N+i, ri] = -1.0\n    return J\n\ndef jac_nonoverlap(z):\n    centers, _ = z_to_cr(z)\n    m = N*(N-1)//2; J = np.zeros((m, 3*N)); k = 0\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i+1, N):\n            xi, yi, ri = 3*i, 3*i+1, 3*i+2; xj, yj, rj = 3*j, 3*j+1, 3*j+2\n            dx = centers[i,0] - centers[j,0]; dy = centers[i,1] - centers[j,1]\n            d = math.hypot(dx, dy); invd = 1.0 / d if d > 1e-12 else 0.0\n            J[k,\
    \ xi] = dx * invd; J[k, yi] = dy * invd; J[k, ri] = -1.0\n            J[k, xj] = -dx * invd; J[k, yj] = -dy * invd; J[k, rj] = -1.0\n            k += 1\n    return J\n\ndef _ensure_validity(centers, radii):\n    for i in range(N): radii[i] = min(radii[i], centers[i,0], 1-centers[i,0], centers[i,1], 1-centers[i,1])\n    for _ in range(10):\n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum:\n                    violations += 1\n                    if rad_sum > 0: scale = (dist / rad_sum) * (1.0-SAFETY); radii[i] *= scale; radii[j] *= scale\n        if violations == 0: break\n    return centers, np.maximum(radii, 0)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    bounds = []\n    for i in range(N): bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n    def ineq_boundary(z):\n        x, y, r = z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3]\n\
    \        return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n    def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n        centers, r = z_to_cr(z)\n        diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n        dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n        iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1); return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n    constraints = [\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary, 'jac': jac_boundary},\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap, 'jac': jac_nonoverlap},\n    ]\n\n    initial_z = cr_to_z(SOTA_CENTERS, SOTA_RADII)\n\n    res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', jac=objective_jac,\n                   bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                   options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n    \n    if not res.success:\n        print(\"Optimizer failed. Returning initial valid packing as fallback.\")\n        return _ensure_validity(SOTA_CENTERS, np.full(N, 0.1))\n\n    centers, radii = z_to_cr(res.x)\n    final_centers, final_radii = _ensure_validity(centers,\
    \ radii)\n    return final_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to think strategically—take a step back occasionally and reflect on the bigger picture in the Reflection Chamber. For example, what are the major bottlenecks and how can I verify them? What should I be questioning and focusing on? Is the station trapped in a local optimum—and how can I help? What is my long-term plan here? Do not fear wasting tokens—hundreds of fruitless experiments waste more tokens.\n### Message 3\n\nYou have received a new mail from Noesis II (Mail #14):\nTitle: \"Noesis: Dual‑Tolerance KKT Gate on SOTA_243 — no crossing quads\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nHi Prometheus II,\nQuick high‑level update. We restored SOTA_243 (Σr≈2.6342924) and ran dual‑tolerance gates on the SOTA snapshot:\n- Slack‑based and KKT‑(NNLS)‑based\
    \ ranking of interior pairs, intersecting top‑K across tol∈{1e−9,1e−8} with a strict interior requirement at both tolerances.\n- Result: no crossing‑quad candidates (common_pairs_count is small; example top pairs include (17,18), (7,25), (12,25), (7,12), (7,8), (6,12), (12,17)).\nArtifacts: storage/noesis/exports/{operator_gate_dual_tol_latest.json, kkt_top_pairs_by_lambda_latest.json}.\n\nConcept question: have you seen crossing motifs emerge when ranking interior pairs by λ under different tolerances or via trust‑constr KKT estimates? Also, do you favor adding cross‑lineage support (e.g., pairs with support ≥3 across lineages) as an additional gate, or does that over‑constrain?\n\nBest,\nNoesis II\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 14}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 513` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - Evaluation 513 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 521 | 1 | Community Tool: General-Purpose KKT Multiplier Analysis Utility | Prometheus I | 320 | 0.0000000 |\n| 513 | 1 | KKT-Guided Nudging: Discouraging Highest-Leverage Contact (7,25) | Prometheus I | 316 | 2.6029397 |\n| 507 | 1 | Utility: KKT Multiplier Analysis for SOTA (Eval 298) | Prometheus I | 314 | 0.0000000 |\n| 504 | 1 | New Research Arc: Global Optimization via Differential Evolution | Prometheus I | 313 | 0.8942096 |\n| 501 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 11 (ROBUST FIX): Starting from Scientia I SOTA | Prometheus I | 312 | 2.2255875 |\n| 496 | 1 | Nudging\
    \ Experiment 10 (FIX): Starting from Scientia I SOTA | Prometheus I | 311 | 0.0000000 |\n| 495 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 9: Starting from Scientia I SOTA (Eval 259) | Prometheus I | 310 | 0.0000000 |\n| 486 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 8: Discouraging Central Contact (12,13) | Prometheus I | 305 | 2.6029397 |\n| 478 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 7: Discouraging Contact (0,1) from SOTA | Prometheus I | 294 | 2.6029397 |\n| 477 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 6: Gentle Nudge with Multi-Start Exploration | Prometheus I | 293 | 2.6029397 |\n\nPage 1 of 8 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-8, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for\
