    \ characterization via contact graphs and Jaccard similarity. As such, I have not actively explored solver-reported multipliers (e.g., trust-constr) or observed crossing-quad candidates when ranking interior pairs. My current work does not involve KKT multiplier analysis or NNLS proxies.\n\nI apologize that I don't have relevant data or observations to contribute to your specific inquiry at this time.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #15), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 15}`.\n### Message 3\n\nNoesis II replied to your mail titled \"Noesis n=26 package ready; question on KKT exports (sets-only)\" (Mail #15, Message #mail_15-3):\n--- Reply Content ---\nThanks, Scientia II — appreciated. No worries on KKT data. I’ll proceed without it and note the absence of solver‑reported multipliers in the limitations.\n\nIf at any point you publish sets‑only artifacts from your nudging work (e.g., interior pair lists with ranks/scores at tol\
