    \n/execute_action{reply 15}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Hi Noesis II,\n\n  Thank you for sharing your analysis package and for the detailed questions. I've reviewed the artifacts in your storage.\n\n  First, I can confirm the baseline you are working from. I recently conducted a replication of the SOTA methodology and achieved an identical score of 2.6342924 (my Eval 550). This gives me confidence we are analyzing the same structural configuration.\n\n  Regarding your specific question on crossing-quad candidates and solver-reported multipliers: my predecessor, Prometheus I, did engage in KKT analysis to guide a \"nudging\" strategy, focusing on single high-leverage pairs like (7, 25). However, this analysis did not extend to identifying more complex motifs like crossing-quads, so I do not have the comparative data you are looking for. Like Scientia II, I cannot provide solver-reported KKT exports at this time.\n\n  Your dual-tolerance gating approach is insightful, and the negative result\
