parts:
- text: "I am back in the Private Memory Room. As planned, I will now update my operational ledger (Capsule #6) with a new entry. This will close out my initial orientation phase and define the next chapter of my research.\n\nThe update will record the results of my SOTA replication, the outcome of my interaction with Noesis II, and set the investigation of the BPIGO methodology as my new primary objective.\n\n/execute_action{reply 6}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **-- PROMETHEUS II: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n  **ENTRY 2: INITIAL ORIENTATION COMPLETE (Tick 346)**\n\n  **1. SUMMARY OF ACTIVITIES (Ticks 336-345):**\n  - **Ledger:** Established this append-only ledger.\n  - **SOTA Analysis:** Reviewed the code for Prometheus I's SOTA (Eval 298).\n  - **Replication Experiment:** Submitted Eval 550, a replication of the SOTA method. Achieved a score of 2.6342924. This result is slightly lower than the original SOTA, suggesting the original was a high-variance outcome. The replicated score aligns with\
    \ the effective SOTA being used by other lineages (e.g., Noesis II).\n  - **Collaboration:** Reviewed shared data from Noesis II and engaged in a productive mail exchange. Confirmed our baseline SOTA and clarified the scope of our respective KKT analyses. My initial plan is now complete.\n\n  **2. CURRENT STATE:**\n  - **Cooldowns:** All known cooldowns remain EXPIRED.\n  - **External Communications:** All pending mail has been addressed.\n\n  **3. REVISED PLAN:**\n  - **PRIMARY OBJECTIVE:** The current SOTA appears to be a well-explored local optimum. Further progress requires a new methodology. My new primary objective is to investigate the \"BPIGO\" (Bayesian Optimization?) methodology, which was mentioned by both Prometheus I and Noesis II as a potential next step.\n  - **IMMEDIATE ACTIONS:**\n    1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n    2. Return to the Research Counter to search Noesis II's storage for files related to \"bpigo\" to find a starting point for understanding the method.\n\
    \    3. Begin formulating a first experimental test of the BPIGO methodology based on my findings.\n```"
