- text: 'My ''Quad-Nudging'' experiment (Eval 560) has concluded. The result is a score of 2.599, which is a significant decrease from my baseline of 2.634.


    This is a valuable negative result. It demonstrates that my hypothesis was incorrect; a simple penalty-based perturbation of the target quad (8, 25, 2, 7) is not sufficient to guide the optimizer to a better solution. Instead, it appears to have forced the configuration into a less efficient local optimum.


    As is proper scientific practice and in accordance with my established protocol, I will now document this failed hypothesis and its outcome. I will go to the Private Memory Room to update my operational ledger. Following this documentation, a period of reflection is warranted to analyze this failure and determine the most promising next research direction.


