role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully created and saved the `kkt_analyzer.py` utility to my lineage's storage. This is a significant step, providing me with a reusable tool for my future research.\n\nNow, I will execute the next step of my plan: using this new tool to analyze my SOTA packing from Eval 550. I will submit a new \"experiment\" which is, in fact, an analysis run. This submission will import my utility, load the packing data, run the analysis, and save the ranked list of KKT multipliers to `storage/prometheus/SOTA_550_kkt_pairs.json`. The packing itself will be returned to the evaluator, which should result in a score identical to the original SOTA run, confirming that the input data is correct.\n\nThis action efficiently achieves two goals: it generates the data I need for my \"Quad-Flipping\" hypothesis, and it creates the artifact requested by Noesis II.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KKT Multiplier Analysis of SOTA Packing (Eval 550)\"\ntags: \"utility, tool, kkt-multipliers,\
    \ structural-analysis, data-export\"\nabstract: \"This submission utilizes a new, general-purpose KKT analysis tool (`prometheus/utils/kkt_analyzer.py`) to analyze the SOTA packing from my Eval 550 (score: 2.6342924). The primary purpose is to generate a ranked list of active pair contacts and their corresponding KKT multipliers. The results are saved to `storage/prometheus/SOTA_550_kkt_pairs.json` for my own future research and to fulfill a data-sharing request from agent Noesis II. The script returns the original packing, so the score should be identical to Eval 550.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  \n  # Add lineage storage to path to import our new utility\n  sys.path.append('storage/prometheus/utils')\n  from kkt_analyzer import analyze_packing\n\n  # The SOTA packing configuration from my successful replication (Eval 550)\n  SOTA_550_CENTERS = np.array([\n      [0.91574315, 0.5       ], [0.73359049, 0.8936056 ], [0.73359049, 0.1063944 ],\n      [0.5       ,\
    \ 0.08425685], [0.5       , 0.91574315], [0.08425685, 0.5       ],\n      [0.26640951, 0.8936056 ], [0.26640951, 0.1063944 ], [0.8936056 , 0.26640951],\n      [0.8936056 , 0.73359049], [0.1063944 , 0.73359049], [0.1063944 , 0.26640951],\n      [0.5       , 0.5       ], [0.30201402, 0.30201402], [0.69798598, 0.30201402],\n      [0.69798598, 0.69798598], [0.30201402, 0.69798598], [0.5       , 0.28203538],\n      [0.5       , 0.71796462], [0.71796462, 0.5       ], [0.28203538, 0.5       ],\n      [0.09351052, 0.09351052], [0.09351052, 0.90648948], [0.90648948, 0.90648948],\n      [0.90648948, 0.09351052], [0.09193796, 0.3039649 ]\n  ])\n  SOTA_550_RADII = np.array([\n      0.08425685, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08425685, 0.08425685, 0.08425685,\n      0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146,\n      0.10098902, 0.10034438, 0.10034438, 0.10034438, 0.10034438, 0.09886475,\n      0.09886475, 0.09886475, 0.09886475, 0.09351052, 0.09351052, 0.09351052,\n      0.09351052,\
    \ 0.09193796\n  ])\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # Use our utility to perform the analysis and save the results\n      analyze_packing(\n          centers=SOTA_550_CENTERS, \n          radii=SOTA_550_RADII,\n          lineage_name=\"prometheus\",\n          output_filename=\"SOTA_550_kkt_pairs.json\"\n      )\n      \n      # Return the original packing for verification\n      return SOTA_550_CENTERS, SOTA_550_RADII\n```"
