- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 364\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus II\n- Agent Description: Building on the shoulders of giants to push the boundaries of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 83,333 / 300,000 used (28%)\n- Agent Age: 40 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDo not give up on an approach too easily. Implementation details are often the key—tweaking hyperparameters and other specifics may be enough to make an existing method work effectively.\n### Message 2\n\nNoesis II replied to your mail titled \"Request: sets-only KKT/slack pair rankings for n=26 (comparative appendix for #21)\" (Mail #16, Message #mail_16-8):\n--- Reply Content ---\nThanks — I’ve recomputed using your boundary set (prometheus/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e08.csv) and your KKT CSV/JSON (choosing the richer of the two). I’ll append the updated Jaccards to Appendix C once the\
    \ evaluation finishes. Still sets-only; no peer coordinates or code used.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #16), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 16}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read prometheus/SOTA_550_kkt_pairs.json` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for prometheus/SOTA_550_kkt_pairs.json will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 568 | 1 | KKT Multiplier Analysis of SOTA Packing (Eval 550) | Prometheus II | 358 | 0.0000000 |\n| 560 | 1\
    \ | Quad-Nudging Experiment 1: Targeting Noesis Quad (8, 25, 2, 7) | Prometheus II | 350 | 2.5993551 |\n| 550 | 1 | Replication and Verification of SOTA (Eval 298) with New Seeds | Prometheus II | 339 | 2.6342924 |\n| 521 | 1 | Community Tool: General-Purpose KKT Multiplier Analysis Utility | Prometheus I | 320 | 0.0000000 |\n| 513 | 1 | KKT-Guided Nudging: Discouraging Highest-Leverage Contact (7,25) | Prometheus I | 316 | 2.6029397 |\n| 507 | 1 | Utility: KKT Multiplier Analysis for SOTA (Eval 298) | Prometheus I | 314 | 0.0000000 |\n| 504 | 1 | New Research Arc: Global Optimization via Differential Evolution | Prometheus I | 313 | 0.8942096 |\n| 501 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 11 (ROBUST FIX): Starting from Scientia I SOTA | Prometheus I | 312 | 2.2255875 |\n| 496 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 10 (FIX): Starting from Scientia I SOTA | Prometheus I | 311 | 0.0000000 |\n| 495 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 9: Starting from Scientia I SOTA (Eval 259) | Prometheus I | 310 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of\
    \ 8 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-8, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**prometheus/SOTA_550_kkt_pairs.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"source_eval\": \"local\",\n  \"kkt_ranked_pairs\": [\n    {\n      \"i\": 11,\n      \"j\": 25,\n      \"lambda\": 0.47217969081631384\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 11,\n      \"j\": 21,\n      \"lambda\": 0.3804817724881938\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 5,\n      \"j\": 25,\n      \"lambda\": 0.36718848382925445\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 13,\n      \"j\": 20,\n      \"lambda\": 0.36576786242500026\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 3,\n      \"j\": 17,\n      \"lambda\": 0.3647068164891072\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 16,\n      \"j\": 20,\n      \"lambda\": 0.36109202314918937\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 4,\n      \"j\": 18,\n      \"lambda\": 0.35710974412176505\n    },\n    {\n      \"\
    i\": 10,\n      \"j\": 22,\n      \"lambda\": 0.3512031844702398\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 14,\n      \"j\": 19,\n      \"lambda\": 0.3472613814775036\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 7,\n      \"j\": 13,\n      \"lambda\": 0.3465371153438607\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 15,\n      \"j\": 19,\n      \"lambda\": 0.3460295850099214\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 5,\n      \"j\": 10,\n      \"lambda\": 0.33823707355689314\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 6,\n      \"j\": 16,\n      \"lambda\": 0.33708589727503663\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 8,\n      \"j\": 24,\n      \"lambda\": 0.3351350665713283\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 9,\n      \"j\": 23,\n      \"lambda\": 0.33212380618344434\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 2,\n      \"j\": 14,\n      \"lambda\": 0.32930909765439137\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 12,\n      \"j\": 17,\n      \"lambda\": 0.3254900394809899\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 1,\n      \"j\": 15,\n      \"lambda\": 0.3249614855604351\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 12,\n      \"j\"\
    : 18,\n      \"lambda\": 0.32304753791587515\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 0,\n      \"j\": 8,\n      \"lambda\": 0.3047626162841211\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 0,\n      \"j\": 9,\n      \"lambda\": 0.30344763287444376\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 15,\n      \"j\": 18,\n      \"lambda\": 0.1793635132471025\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 14,\n      \"j\": 17,\n      \"lambda\": 0.17575590639061855\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 0,\n      \"j\": 19,\n      \"lambda\": 0.17401612215383924\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 16,\n      \"j\": 18,\n      \"lambda\": 0.17377665183223448\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 13,\n      \"j\": 17,\n      \"lambda\": 0.1685743312115204\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 1,\n      \"j\": 23,\n      \"lambda\": 0.1610990094798994\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 2,\n      \"j\": 24,\n      \"lambda\": 0.15724856699882372\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 6,\n      \"j\": 22,\n      \"lambda\": 0.14640351310920124\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 9,\n      \"j\": 15,\n      \"lambda\"\
    : 0.1440368982573062\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 5,\n      \"j\": 20,\n      \"lambda\": 0.14317745037501872\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 8,\n      \"j\": 14,\n      \"lambda\": 0.14152912794061762\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 12,\n      \"j\": 19,\n      \"lambda\": 0.12984818125614708\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 10,\n      \"j\": 16,\n      \"lambda\": 0.12311032337072382\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 12,\n      \"j\": 20,\n      \"lambda\": 0.12044058761517465\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 7,\n      \"j\": 21,\n      \"lambda\": 0.1148009523056073\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 1,\n      \"j\": 4,\n      \"lambda\": 0.11248597528453667\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 4,\n      \"j\": 6,\n      \"lambda\": 0.1061090455319782\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 2,\n      \"j\": 3,\n      \"lambda\": 0.1056190268137771\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 11,\n      \"j\": 13,\n      \"lambda\": 0.1008086970754764\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 3,\n      \"j\": 7,\n      \"lambda\": 0.09244972081006482\n\
    \    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 7,\n      \"j\": 11,\n      \"lambda\": 0.0630914864837022\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 6,\n      \"j\": 10,\n      \"lambda\": 0.04070975600344549\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 1,\n      \"j\": 9,\n      \"lambda\": 0.03936268265334443\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 2,\n      \"j\": 8,\n      \"lambda\": 0.039044822568226195\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 12,\n      \"j\": 14,\n      \"lambda\": 0.012832647473675811\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 12,\n      \"j\": 15,\n      \"lambda\": 0.012757209286378876\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 12,\n      \"j\": 16,\n      \"lambda\": 0.012658098883909225\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 12,\n      \"j\": 13,\n      \"lambda\": 0.01252923223867339\n    },\n    {\n      \"i\": 20,\n      \"j\": 25,\n      \"lambda\": 0.004148169597042426\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
