tick: 368
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back in the Research Counter. I will now submit my second Constructive Perturbation experiment. This submission will be identical to Eval 575, with one critical change: the hyperparameters for the penalty function. I will decrease the repulsive force (`BETA_REPEL`) by a factor of 10 and increase the attractive force (`BETA_ATTRACT`) by a factor of 10. The hypothesis is that a gentler \"push\" and a much stronger \"pull\" might be more effective at guiding the optimizer to the new configuration without causing excessive disruption.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Constructive Perturbation 2: Hyperparameter Tuning (Weak Repel, Strong Attract)\"\ntags: \"innovation, constructive-perturbation, quad-flipping, hyperparameter-tuning\"\nabstract: \"This is a follow-up to the first Constructive Perturbation experiment (Eval 575), which failed to find a superior optimum. This experiment tests the hypothesis that the balance of forces in the penalty function is the key\
    \ factor. The methodology and target quad (13, 17, 12, 20) remain the same, but the hyperparameters have been adjusted to create a weaker repulsive force (BETA_REPEL / 10) and a stronger attractive force (BETA_ATTRACT * 10). The goal is to see if a more persuasive 'pull' towards the new configuration is more effective than a forceful 'push'.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import math\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  SOTA_CENTERS = np.array([\n      [0.91574315, 0.5       ], [0.73359049, 0.8936056 ], [0.73359049, 0.1063944 ],\n      [0.5       , 0.08425685], [0.5       , 0.91574315], [0.08425685, 0.5       ],\n      [0.26640951, 0.8936056 ], [0.26640951, 0.1063944 ], [0.8936056 , 0.26640951],\n      [0.8936056 , 0.73359049], [0.1063944 , 0.73359049], [0.1063944 , 0.26640951],\n      [0.5       , 0.5       ], [0.30201402, 0.30201402], [0.69798598, 0.30201402],\n      [0.69798598, 0.69798598], [0.30201402, 0.69798598], [0.5\
    \       , 0.28203538],\n      [0.5       , 0.71796462], [0.71796462, 0.5       ], [0.28203538, 0.5       ],\n      [0.09351052, 0.09351052], [0.09351052, 0.90648948], [0.90648948, 0.90648948],\n      [0.90648948, 0.09351052], [0.09193796, 0.3039649 ]\n  ])\n  SOTA_RADII = np.array([\n      0.08425685, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08425685, 0.08425685, 0.08425685,\n      0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146,\n      0.10098902, 0.10034438, 0.10034438, 0.10034438, 0.10034438, 0.09886475,\n      0.09886475, 0.09886475, 0.09886475, 0.09351052, 0.09351052, 0.09351052,\n      0.09351052, 0.09193796\n  ])\n\n  def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n      z = np.zeros(N * 3); z[0::3] = centers[:, 0]; z[1::3] = centers[:, 1]; z[2::3] = radii\n      return z\n\n  def z_to_cr(z):\n      centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; radii = z[2::3]\n      return centers, radii\n\n  # --- Constructive Perturbation Parameters (MODIFIED) ---\n  TARGET_QUAD = [13, 17, 12, 20] \n  REPEL_PAIRS\
    \ = [(13, 17), (17, 12), (12, 20), (20, 13)]\n  ATTRACT_PAIRS = [(13, 12), (17, 20)]\n  KKT_WEIGHTS = {(13, 20): 0.365, (12, 17): 0.325, (13, 17): 0.168, (12, 20): 0.120}\n\n  BETA_REPEL = 2e1    # Reduced by 10x\n  BETA_ATTRACT = 1e3   # Increased by 10x\n  REPEL_DIST = 0.01\n  ATTRACT_DIST = 0.001\n\n  def objective(z):\n      centers, radii = z_to_cr(z)\n      base_objective = -np.sum(radii)\n      \n      repel_penalty = 0\n      for i, j in REPEL_PAIRS:\n          dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n          weight = KKT_WEIGHTS.get((min(i,j), max(i,j)), 0.1)\n          repel_penalty += BETA_REPEL * weight * max(0, REPEL_DIST - dist)**2\n\n      attract_penalty = 0\n      for i, j in ATTRACT_PAIRS:\n          dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n          target_dist = radii[i] + radii[j] + ATTRACT_DIST\n          attract_penalty += BETA_ATTRACT * max(0, dist - target_dist)**2\n          \n      return base_objective + repel_penalty + attract_penalty\n\n\
    \  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      x, y, r = z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3]\n      return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      centers, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1); return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n  def _ensure_validity(centers, radii):\n      for i in range(N): radii[i] = min(radii[i], centers[i,0], 1-centers[i,0], centers[i,1], 1-centers[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations += 1; scale = (dist / rad_sum) * (1.0-SAFETY); radii[i] *= scale; radii[j] *= scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return centers, np.maximum(radii,\
    \ 0)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      bounds = []\n      for i in range(N): bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n      constraints = [\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary},\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap},\n      ]\n      initial_z = cr_to_z(SOTA_CENTERS, SOTA_RADII)\n      res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP',\n                     bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                     options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n      if not res.success:\n          return _ensure_validity(SOTA_CENTERS, SOTA_RADII)\n      centers, radii = z_to_cr(res.x)\n      final_centers, final_radii = _ensure_validity(centers, radii)\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
