tick: 372
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Research Counter and ready to launch my new research arc. As planned, this first submission will be a proof-of-concept for the Simulated Annealing with Radius Growth methodology.\n\nThe implementation will be straightforward:\n1.  Start with 26 very small, non-overlapping circles.\n2.  Iteratively propose random moves for individual circles.\n3.  Calculate the \"energy\" of the system as the sum of squared overlaps.\n4.  Accept moves based on the Metropolis criterion, governed by a slowly decreasing temperature.\n5.  After a set number of moves, slightly increase the radius of all circles and repeat the annealing process.\n6.  The number of iterations will be kept relatively low for this first run to ensure it completes within the time limit and to validate the basic logic.\n\nThis experiment represents a complete departure from previous SOTA methods and has the potential to discover entirely new packing configurations.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"\
    Simulated Annealing with Radius Growth - Experiment 1 (Proof of Concept)\"\ntags: \"innovation, global-search, simulated-annealing, new-methodology\"\nabstract: \"This submission marks the beginning of a new research arc, abandoning local, gradient-based optimization in favor of a global search method. It implements a proof-of-concept Simulated Annealing algorithm. The system starts with small, randomly placed circles. It then iteratively attempts random moves, accepting them based on the Metropolis criterion to minimize overlaps. Periodically, the radii of all circles are uniformly increased, and the annealing process is repeated. This first experiment uses a limited number of iterations to validate the approach and establish a baseline for this new methodology.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import math\n  import random\n\n  N = 26\n\n  def calculate_energy(centers, radius):\n      \"\"\"Calculates the 'energy' of the system, defined as sum of squared overlaps.\"\"\"\n    \
    \  energy = 0\n      # Boundary overlaps\n      for i in range(N):\n          energy += max(0, centers[i, 0] + radius - 1)**2\n          energy += max(0, centers[i, 1] + radius - 1)**2\n          energy += max(0, -centers[i, 0] + radius)**2\n          energy += max(0, -centers[i, 1] + radius)**2\n      \n      # Pair overlaps\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j])**2)\n              overlap = 2 * radius - math.sqrt(dist_sq) if dist_sq > 0 else 2 * radius\n              energy += max(0, overlap)**2\n      return energy\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # --- Hyperparameters ---\n      initial_radius = 0.01\n      radius_growth_factor = 1.005\n      n_growth_steps = 150\n      \n      initial_temp = 1.0\n      cooling_factor = 0.99\n      moves_per_step = 5000\n      max_move_dist = 0.1\n\n      # --- Initialization ---\n      np.random.seed(370)\n      random.seed(370)\n      centers = np.random.rand(N,\
    \ 2)\n      radius = initial_radius\n      \n      current_energy = calculate_energy(centers, radius)\n      temp = initial_temp\n      \n      best_centers = np.copy(centers)\n      best_radius = radius\n      \n      # --- Main Loop ---\n      for step in range(n_growth_steps):\n          # Annealing phase\n          for _ in range(moves_per_step):\n              i = random.randint(0, N - 1)\n              old_pos = np.copy(centers[i])\n              \n              move = (np.random.rand(2) - 0.5) * max_move_dist\n              centers[i] += move\n              \n              new_energy = calculate_energy(centers, radius)\n              delta_e = new_energy - current_energy\n              \n              if delta_e < 0 or random.random() < math.exp(-delta_e / temp):\n                  current_energy = new_energy\n              else:\n                  centers[i] = old_pos # Revert move\n          \n          # Cool down temperature\n          temp *= cooling_factor\n          \n\
    \          # Grow radii if system is stable (no overlaps)\n          final_energy = calculate_energy(centers, radius)\n          if final_energy < 1e-9:\n              best_centers = np.copy(centers)\n              best_radius = radius\n              radius *= radius_growth_factor\n          else:\n              # If we can't stabilize, stop growing\n              break\n\n      # Final validation and return\n      final_radii = np.full(N, best_radius)\n      return best_centers, final_radii\n```"
