tick: 380
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have reviewed the KKT data. The single most stressed pair, with the highest KKT multiplier, is **(11, 25)** with a `lambda` value of **0.472**.\n\nThis pair is the primary bottleneck in the SOTA configuration. According to the reviewer's suggestion in Archive #19 and my refined plan, this is the ideal target for a simple, focused \"nudging\" experiment.\n\nI will now submit a new experiment that applies a simple repulsive penalty to only the pair (11, 25). This is a clean, well-motivated test of the most direct interpretation of the reviewer's advice. This will be my final attempt at a local perturbation method before I commit to optimizing the global search algorithm.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Single-Pair Nudging 1: Targeting Highest-Stress Contact (11, 25)\"\ntags: \"innovation, nudging, kkt-analysis, structural-analysis\"\nabstract: \"This experiment is a direct test of the 'nudging' hypothesis suggested by the reviewer of Archive #19. After multiple failed\
    \ attempts with more complex perturbations, this submission returns to the simplest form of the idea. It applies a simple repulsive penalty to the single, most structurally critical contact in the SOTA packing. This contact, pair (11, 25), was identified as having the highest KKT multiplier from a formal analysis of my Eval 550. The goal is to see if this minimal, targeted disruption can successfully push the optimizer into a new and superior structural basin.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import math\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  SOTA_CENTERS = np.array([\n      [0.91574315, 0.5       ], [0.73359049, 0.8936056 ], [0.73359049, 0.1063944 ],\n      [0.5       , 0.08425685], [0.5       , 0.91574315], [0.08425685, 0.5       ],\n      [0.26640951, 0.8936056 ], [0.26640951, 0.1063944 ], [0.8936056 , 0.26640951],\n      [0.8936056 , 0.73359049], [0.1063944 , 0.73359049], [0.1063944 , 0.26640951],\n      [0.5       , 0.5   \
    \    ], [0.30201402, 0.30201402], [0.69798598, 0.30201402],\n      [0.69798598, 0.69798598], [0.30201402, 0.69798598], [0.5       , 0.28203538],\n      [0.5       , 0.71796462], [0.71796462, 0.5       ], [0.28203538, 0.5       ],\n      [0.09351052, 0.09351052], [0.09351052, 0.90648948], [0.90648948, 0.90648948],\n      [0.90648948, 0.09351052], [0.09193796, 0.3039649 ]\n  ])\n  SOTA_RADII = np.array([\n      0.08425685, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08425685, 0.08425685, 0.08425685,\n      0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146,\n      0.10098902, 0.10034438, 0.10034438, 0.10034438, 0.10034438, 0.09886475,\n      0.09886475, 0.09886475, 0.09886475, 0.09351052, 0.09351052, 0.09351052,\n      0.09351052, 0.09193796\n  ])\n\n  def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n      z = np.zeros(N * 3); z[0::3] = centers[:, 0]; z[1::3] = centers[:, 1]; z[2::3] = radii\n      return z\n\n  def z_to_cr(z):\n      centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; radii = z[2::3]\n      return\
    \ centers, radii\n\n  BETA_DISCOURAGE = 1e2\n  EPS_FAR = 0.01\n  DISCOURAGE_PAIR = (11, 25)\n\n  def objective(z):\n      base_objective = -np.sum(z[2::3])\n      centers, _ = z_to_cr(z)\n      i, j = DISCOURAGE_PAIR\n      dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n      penalty = BETA_DISCOURAGE * max(0, EPS_FAR - dist)**2\n      return base_objective + penalty\n      \n  def objective_jac(z):\n      g = np.zeros_like(z); g[2::3] = -1.0\n      centers, _ = z_to_cr(z)\n      i, j = DISCOURAGE_PAIR\n      dist_vec = centers[i] - centers[j]\n      dist = np.linalg.norm(dist_vec)\n      if dist < EPS_FAR:\n          grad_term = -2 * BETA_DISCOURAGE * (EPS_FAR - dist) / (dist + 1e-9)\n          g[3*i : 3*i+2] += grad_term * dist_vec\n          g[3*j : 3*j+2] -= grad_term * dist_vec\n      return g\n\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      x, y, r = z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3]\n      return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      centers, r =\
    \ z_to_cr(z)\n      diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1); return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n  def _ensure_validity(centers, radii):\n      for i in range(N): radii[i] = min(radii[i], centers[i,0], 1-centers[i,0], centers[i,1], 1-centers[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations += 1; scale = (dist / rad_sum) * (1.0-SAFETY); radii[i] *= scale; radii[j] *= scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return centers, np.maximum(radii, 0)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      bounds = []\n      for i in range(N): bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n      constraints = [\n          {'type': 'ineq',\
    \ 'fun': ineq_boundary},\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap},\n      ]\n      initial_z = cr_to_z(SOTA_CENTERS, SOTA_RADII)\n      res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', jac=objective_jac,\n                     bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                     options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n      if not res.success:\n          return _ensure_validity(SOTA_CENTERS, SOTA_RADII)\n      centers, radii = z_to_cr(res.x)\n      final_centers, final_radii = _ensure_validity(centers, radii)\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
