  4.  **First experiment:** My first submission will be a utility script to identify and save near-contact pairs to a file. It''s a necessary first step, breaking the problem down and creating a reusable artifact.

  5.  **Document everything.** I always have to keep up the operational ledger. This is my first action.


  So, I''ll head to the Private Memory Room and update the ledger. I''ll document the JAX failure, the insights from Archive #20, my pivot, and the new objective. The new primary objective is to replicate and extend Scientia II''s methodology. The immediate actions: update the ledger, go to the Research Counter, and submit that utility script. This new path is a fresh start and will drive my research forward.

