tick: 389
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Research Counter. I will ignore the mail from Noesis. My objective is to create a utility script to identify \"near-contact\" pairs in my SOTA packing (Eval 550), adopting the methodology from Scientia II's successful research (Archive #20).\n\nThis script will analyze the packing and save a JSON file containing the list of identified pairs to my lineage storage. This will provide the targets for my new experimental arc.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Identify Near-Contact Pairs in SOTA Packing (Eval 550)\"\ntags: \"utility, structural-analysis, near-contact\"\nabstract: \"This is the first step in adopting the successful 'near-contact encouragement' methodology from Scientia II (Archive #20). This script analyzes my SOTA packing from Eval 550 (score ~2.634) to identify all 'near-contact' pairs. A pair is a near-contact if it is not touching (distance > r_i + r_j + 1e-8) but the separation between circle edges is less than or equal to 0.01.\
    \ The resulting list of pairs will be saved to `storage/prometheus/SOTA_550_near_contacts.json` to serve as targets for a new series of nudging experiments.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import json\n  import os\n  import math\n\n  N = 26\n\n  SOTA_550_CENTERS = np.array([\n      [0.91574315, 0.5       ], [0.73359049, 0.8936056 ], [0.73359049, 0.1063944 ],\n      [0.5       , 0.08425685], [0.5       , 0.91574315], [0.08425685, 0.5       ],\n      [0.26640951, 0.8936056 ], [0.26640951, 0.1063944 ], [0.8936056 , 0.26640951],\n      [0.8936056 , 0.73359049], [0.1063944 , 0.73359049], [0.1063944 , 0.26640951],\n      [0.5       , 0.5       ], [0.30201402, 0.30201402], [0.69798598, 0.30201402],\n      [0.69798598, 0.69798598], [0.30201402, 0.69798598], [0.5       , 0.28203538],\n      [0.5       , 0.71796462], [0.71796462, 0.5       ], [0.28203538, 0.5       ],\n      [0.09351052, 0.09351052], [0.09351052, 0.90648948], [0.90648948, 0.90648948],\n      [0.90648948, 0.09351052], [0.09193796,\
    \ 0.3039649 ]\n  ])\n  SOTA_550_RADII = np.array([\n      0.08425685, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08425685, 0.08425685, 0.08425685,\n      0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146, 0.08383146,\n      0.10098902, 0.10034438, 0.10034438, 0.10034438, 0.10034438, 0.09886475,\n      0.09886475, 0.09886475, 0.09886475, 0.09351052, 0.09351052, 0.09351052,\n      0.09351052, 0.09193796\n  ])\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # --- Parameters from Scientia II, Archive #20 ---\n      CONTACT_TOL = 1e-8\n      NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD = 0.01\n      \n      near_contact_pairs = []\n      \n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(SOTA_550_CENTERS[i] - SOTA_550_CENTERS[j])\n              rad_sum = SOTA_550_RADII[i] + SOTA_550_RADII[j]\n              separation = dist - rad_sum\n              \n              # Check if it's NOT an active contact\n              is_not_contact = separation > CONTACT_TOL\n           \
    \   \n              # Check if it IS a near-contact\n              is_near_contact = separation <= NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD\n              \n              if is_not_contact and is_near_contact:\n                  near_contact_pairs.append({\n                      \"i\": i,\n                      \"j\": j,\n                      \"separation\": separation\n                  })\n      \n      # Sort by separation, closest first\n      near_contact_pairs.sort(key=lambda x: x[\"separation\"])\n\n      # Save to lineage storage\n      lineage_name = \"prometheus\"\n      output_filename = \"SOTA_550_near_contacts.json\"\n      base_path = f'storage/{lineage_name}/'\n      os.makedirs(base_path, exist_ok=True)\n      output_path = os.path.join(base_path, output_filename)\n      \n      with open(output_path, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump({\n              \"source_eval\": 550,\n              \"near_contact_pairs\": near_contact_pairs\n          }, f, indent=2)\n          \n      print(f\"Identified\
    \ and saved {len(near_contact_pairs)} near-contact pairs to {output_path}\")\n\n      # This is a utility run, return the original packing\n      return SOTA_550_CENTERS, SOTA_550_RADII\n```"
