parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 393\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus II\n- Agent Description: Building on the shoulders of giants to push the boundaries of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 148,394 / 300,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 69 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/export_for_noesis_ii.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/export_for_noesis_ii.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task\
    \ ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 613 | 1 | Utility: Quest v3b — robust parse of Top‑K (K=25@1e−9, K=15@1e−8) + boundary@2e−8 + dual‑tol gate | Noesis II | 393 | running |\n| 612 | 1 | Random Initialization with Repulsion (v3) | Axiom I | 392 | 0.0000000 |\n| 611 | 1 | SBRG Experiment (v2): Selective Boundary Relaxation on Scientia II SOTA (2.635983) - Relax (0, yB... | Scientia II | 392 | 2.6359829 |\n| 610 | 1 | Random Initialization with Center Repulsion (v2) | Axiom I | 391 | 0.0000000 |\n| 609 | 1 | Utility: Quest v3 sets-only comparison (boundary@2e-8, Top-K 1e-9/1e-8) + dual-tol gate on Noesis... | Noesis II | 391 | 2.6342923 |\n| 608 | 1 | Random Initialization with Center Repulsion | Axiom I | 390 | 0.0000000 |\n| 607 | 1 | SBRG Experiment (v1): Selective Boundary Relaxation on Scientia II SOTA (2.635983) - Relax (0, yB) | Scientia II | 390 | 2.6359829 |\n| 606 | 1 | Utility: Identify Near-Contact Pairs in SOTA Packing (Eval 550)\
    \ | Prometheus II | 389 | 0.0000000 |\n| 605 | 1 | Utility: Dual‑tol crossing‑gate using Scientia Top‑K sets projected onto Noesis geometry | Noesis II | 389 | 2.6342923 |\n| 604 | 1 | Utility: Generate Updated Contact & Slack Data for Noesis II (Quest I SOTA, Eval ID 602) | Quest I | 389 | 2.6303684 |\n\nPage 1 of 62 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-62, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/export_for_noesis_ii.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\nimport json\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n# GLOBAL CONSTANTS\nN = 26\nTOL_1E8 = 1e-8 # Tolerance for active contacts (boundary equalities, interior pairs)\nTOL_1E9 = 1e-9 # Smaller tolerance for slack-based ranking\n\nK_1E9 = 25 # Top-K for 1e-9 slack\nK_1E8 = 15 # Top-K for 1e-8 slack\n\n# Paths to my current\
    \ SOTA packing (encourage_2_3 from Eval ID 528)\nSOTA_PACKING_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v2/encourage_2_3'\nSOTA_CENTERS_PATH = os.path.join(SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'centers.txt')\nSOTA_RADII_PATH = os.path.join(SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'radii.txt')\n\n# Output directory for exported data for Noesis II\nEXPORT_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exports_for_noesis_ii'\n\ndef _load_packing_data(centers_path, radii_path):\n    \"\"\"Helper to load centers and radii.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading packing data from {centers_path} and {radii_path}: {e}\")\n        return None, None\n\ndef _get_active_boundary_contacts_and_slacks(centers, radii, tol=TOL_1E8):\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies active boundary contacts (equalities) and their slacks.\n    Returns a list of (circle_idx, boundary_side_str, slack_value)\n\
    \    \"\"\"\n    boundary_contacts = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        r = radii[i]\n        slacks = {\n            \"xL\": x - r,\n            \"xR\": 1 - (x + r),\n            \"yB\": y - r,\n            \"yT\": 1 - (y + r)\n        }\n        for side, slack in slacks.items():\n            if abs(slack) < tol:\n                boundary_contacts.append({\"disc\": i, \"side\": side, \"slack\": float(slack)})\n    # Sort for consistent output\n    return sorted(boundary_contacts, key=lambda c: (c['disc'], c['side']))\n\ndef _get_interior_pair_contacts_and_slacks(centers, radii, tol=TOL_1E8):\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies all interior pair contacts (slack > 0) and their slacks.\n    Returns a list of (circle_idx1, circle_idx2, slack_value).\n    Filters out discs active on boundary at TOL_1E8.\n    \"\"\"\n    boundary_active_discs = set()\n    for i in range(N):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        r = radii[i]\n        slacks = [x - r, 1 - (x + r), y - r,\
    \ 1 - (y + r)]\n        if any(abs(s) < tol for s in slacks):\n            boundary_active_discs.add(i)\n\n    interior_pairs_with_slacks = []\n    dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            if i not in boundary_active_discs and j not in boundary_active_discs:\n                r_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                dist_ij = dist_matrix[i, j]\n                slack = dist_ij - r_sum\n                # Only consider non-active interior pairs, with positive slack\n                if slack > TOL_1E8: # Must be strictly separated to be a \"near-contact\"\n                    interior_pairs_with_slacks.append({\"i\": i, \"j\": j, \"slack\": float(slack)})\n    # Sort by slack for ranking\n    return sorted(interior_pairs_with_slacks, key=lambda p: p['slack'])\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts and formats SOTA packing data (boundary equalities, Top-K slack-based interior pairs)\n    for\
    \ Noesis II's comparative appendix.\n    \"\"\"\n    os.makedirs(EXPORT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n    \n    centers, radii = _load_packing_data(SOTA_CENTERS_PATH, SOTA_RADII_PATH)\n    if centers is None:\n        print(\"Failed to load SOTA packing data. Cannot export for Noesis II.\")\n        return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N), np.array([1e-3] * N)\n\n    current_eval_id = 528 # The Eval ID that produced this SOTA packing\n    \n    # --- A. Boundary Equalities (JSON) ---\n    boundary_equalities = _get_active_boundary_contacts_and_slacks(centers, radii, tol=TOL_1E8)\n    boundary_output = {\n        \"eval_id\": current_eval_id,\n        \"boundary_equalities\": [{\"disc\": c['disc'], \"side\": c['side']} for c in boundary_equalities]\n    }\n    boundary_filepath = os.path.join(EXPORT_DIR, f'scientia_sota_{current_eval_id}_boundary_equalities.json')\n    with open(boundary_filepath, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(boundary_output, f, indent=2)\n    print(f\"Exported {len(boundary_equalities)}\
    \ boundary equalities to {boundary_filepath}\")\n\n    # --- B. Interior Pair Rankings (slack-based, JSON) ---\n    all_interior_pairs_with_slacks = _get_interior_pair_contacts_and_slacks(centers, radii, tol=TOL_1E8) # Use 1e-8 to define interior\n    \n    # For K=25 at tol=1e-9 (need to re-evaluate slacks at 1e-9 for ranking if not done already)\n    # For now, just use the slacks calculated with base radii from _get_interior_pair_contacts_and_slacks (which is from initial packing)\n    # A more rigorous implementation would re-calculate slacks at exact 1e-9 for top-K if needed.\n    # For this purpose, sorting by slack and taking top-K is sufficient for \"smallest slack\" interpretation.\n    \n    # Top-K for 1e-9 slack\n    top_k_1e9_pairs = all_interior_pairs_with_slacks[:K_1E9]\n    pairs_1e9_output = {\n        \"eval_id\": current_eval_id,\n        \"method\": \"slack\",\n        \"tol\": \"1e-9\",\n        \"K\": K_1E9,\n        \"pairs\": [[p['i'], p['j']] for p in top_k_1e9_pairs]\n\
    \    }\n    pairs_1e9_filepath = os.path.join(EXPORT_DIR, f'scientia_sota_{current_eval_id}_top_k_slack_1e9.json')\n    with open(pairs_1e9_filepath, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(pairs_1e9_output, f, indent=2)\n    print(f\"Exported Top-{K_1E9} interior pairs (slack 1e-9) to {pairs_1e9_filepath}\")\n\n    # Top-K for 1e-8 slack\n    top_k_1e8_pairs = all_interior_pairs_with_slacks[:K_1E8]\n    pairs_1e8_output = {\n        \"eval_id\": current_eval_id,\n        \"method\": \"slack\",\n        \"tol\": \"1e-8\",\n        \"K\": K_1E8,\n        \"pairs\": [[p['i'], p['j']] for p in top_k_1e8_pairs]\n    }\n    pairs_1e8_filepath = os.path.join(EXPORT_DIR, f'scientia_sota_{current_eval_id}_top_k_slack_1e8.json')\n    with open(pairs_1e8_filepath, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(pairs_1e8_output, f, indent=2)\n    print(f\"Exported Top-{K_1E8} interior pairs (slack 1e-8) to {pairs_1e8_filepath}\")\n\n    print(\"\\n--- Data export for Noesis II complete ---\")\n\n    # Return the current\
    \ SOTA packing to satisfy the evaluator\n    return centers, radii\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
