tick: 395
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus II in the Research Counter. My current objective is to replicate Scientia II's \"near-contact encouragement\" methodology. My own SOTA packing did not contain any near-contacts, so I have successfully located and read the centers and radii files for Scientia II's SOTA packing, which serves as a valid baseline. I will ignore the ongoing mail correspondence as it is not relevant to my immediate task.\n\nMy past experiments with local perturbations have consistently failed, which has led me to this new, more promising, and empirically validated research arc. My future plan is to first verify that I can identify the near-contacts in Scientia II's packing, and then to begin a systematic series of experiments to encourage the formation of those contacts, one by one.\n\nI now have all the data necessary to proceed. I will submit a new utility run that uses Scientia II's packing data as input to my near-contact identification script. This will validate my ability to work\
    \ with their baseline and will generate the crucial list of targets for my subsequent experiments.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Identify Near-Contacts in Scientia II SOTA Packing (Eval 528)\"\ntags: \"utility, structural-analysis, near-contact, replication\"\nabstract: \"After failing to find near-contacts in my own SOTA (Eval 606), I am now analyzing Scientia II's SOTA packing from Eval 528 (score ~2.6359). This script uses their publicly available packing data as input for my near-contact identification logic. The goal is to verify that their packing contains identifiable near-contact pairs and to generate a list of these pairs to be used as targets in my upcoming 'near-contact encouragement' experimental series. The results will be saved to `storage/prometheus/scientia_SOTA_528_near_contacts.json`.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import json\n  import os\n\n  N = 26\n\n  # Data loaded from Scientia's storage\n  SCIENTIA_SOTA_CENTERS = np.array([\n\
    \      [8.492626245490325632e-02, 8.492626245489955095e-02], [1.332585727708142376e-01, 2.976904749108396642e-01],\n      [7.886037291596154075e-02, 5.027155537958869491e-01], [1.302211010652318812e-01, 7.053905112181719783e-01],\n      [8.463950069576857416e-02, 9.153604993042284699e-01], [2.739528396239510055e-01, 1.051825602687500166e-01],\n      [3.816658444526486726e-01, 2.973903963009784102e-01], [2.753426167714373429e-01, 5.044682393256384456e-01],\n      [3.869235534096087670e-01, 7.052539409510502066e-01], [2.747832833508189743e-01, 8.932098553714216127e-01],\n      [4.825955822105374993e-01, 1.034672333579526315e-01], [5.960427019081339095e-01, 2.730942856883976089e-01],\n      [5.299634197531902791e-01, 5.013319244965969146e-01], [5.976347963876644798e-01, 7.283701485139996157e-01],\n      [4.846008026519129652e-01, 8.969394798584140460e-01], [6.820800429325878378e-01, 9.615133404576799159e-02],\n      [7.629588636540003410e-01, 2.406475984390707423e-01], [7.420494434605940937e-01,\
    \ 4.047802670602677622e-01],\n      [7.424170495016405580e-01, 5.966412163973151550e-01], [6.832585349730860846e-01, 9.042676706929789754e-01],\n      [8.888438205895518029e-01, 1.111561794104394679e-01], [9.074079050485648335e-01, 3.140569780132145827e-01],\n      [9.060726627225502705e-01, 5.005716308609604592e-01], [9.076084484290364296e-01, 6.868841900295953318e-01],\n      [8.892209872092887712e-01, 8.892209872092843304e-01], [7.636735693833809346e-01, 7.602894720724653332e-01]\n  ])\n  SCIENTIA_SOTA_RADII = np.array([\n      8.492625245489955621e-02, 1.332585627708142428e-01, 7.886036291596154602e-02, 1.302210910652318865e-01,\n      8.463949069576857942e-02, 1.051825502687500219e-01, 1.151488751600189958e-01, 1.176296830465418664e-01,\n      1.120770839502557153e-01, 1.067901346285783926e-01, 1.034672233579526368e-01, 1.006003628187135401e-01,\n      1.370104251237446169e-01, 9.989834559275019565e-02, 1.030605101415859592e-01, 9.615132404576799685e-02,\n      6.944018871125764991e-02,\
    \ 9.601897075825123473e-02, 9.584232074550398661e-02, 9.573231930702102987e-02,\n      1.111561694104394732e-01, 9.259208495143517181e-02, 9.392732727744973475e-02, 9.239154157096357567e-02,\n      1.107790027907112340e-01, 6.918067135723383887e-02\n  ])\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      CONTACT_TOL = 1e-8\n      NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD = 0.01\n      near_contact_pairs = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(SCIENTIA_SOTA_CENTERS[i] - SCIENTIA_SOTA_CENTERS[j])\n              rad_sum = SCIENTIA_SOTA_RADII[i] + SCIENTIA_SOTA_RADII[j]\n              separation = dist - rad_sum\n              if separation > CONTACT_TOL and separation <= NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD:\n                  near_contact_pairs.append({\"i\": i, \"j\": j, \"separation\": separation})\n      \n      near_contact_pairs.sort(key=lambda x: x[\"separation\"])\n\n      lineage_name = \"prometheus\"\n      output_filename = \"scientia_SOTA_528_near_contacts.json\"\
    \n      output_path = f'storage/{lineage_name}/{output_filename}'\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(output_path), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(output_path, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump({\"source_eval\": 528, \"near_contact_pairs\": near_contact_pairs}, f, indent=2)\n      print(f\"Identified and saved {len(near_contact_pairs)} near-contact pairs to {output_path}\")\n\n      return SCIENTIA_SOTA_CENTERS, SCIENTIA_SOTA_RADII\n```"
