tick: 400
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus II, in the Research Counter. I have just achieved a new SOTA and have a clear plan to build on it. The ongoing mail exchange between Scientia II and Noesis II is noted as a source of valuable ambient information about advanced structural analysis, but it does not require my direct action.\n\nMy immediate priority is to capitalize on my breakthrough. My reflection on my own lineage's successes (Archive #19) and my recent successful replication of Scientia II's method (Eval 620) has led to a powerful synthesis strategy. I will now apply the \"Exhaustive Seeding\" methodology, which my predecessor used to find deep optima, to my new SOTA configuration. Instead of generating a grid-based seed, I will perform a multi-start search by applying various levels of random jitter to my new SOTA packing. This will thoroughly explore the local landscape of this new, promising structural basin.\n\nThis experiment represents the synthesis of the station's leading research paradigms\
    \ and is the most logical next step to push the frontier even further.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Deepening: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New SOTA (from Eval 620)\"\ntags: \"sota-push, exhaustive-search, jitter-seeding, methodology-synthesis\"\nabstract: \"This experiment capitalizes on the new SOTA packing discovered in Eval 620 (score ~2.635983). It applies my lineage's proven 'Exhaustive Seeding' methodology to this new configuration. Instead of a grid-based seed, this method performs a multi-start local search by applying multiple levels of random jitter to the new SOTA's centers. The hypothesis is that this will identify an even deeper optimum within the new, high-potential structural basin discovered by the 'near-contact encouragement' method. This submission synthesizes the station's two most successful strategies: landscape traversal (Scientia II) and deep local search (Prometheus I).\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\
    \  import math\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  # My new SOTA packing from Eval 620\n  SOTA_CENTERS = np.array([\n      [0.08492625, 0.08492625], [0.13325856, 0.29769047], [0.07886036, 0.50271555],\n      [0.13022109, 0.70539051], [0.08463949, 0.9153605 ], [0.27395284, 0.10518255],\n      [0.38166585, 0.2973904 ], [0.27534262, 0.50446824], [0.38692355, 0.70525394],\n      [0.27478328, 0.89320986], [0.48259558, 0.10346722], [0.5960427 , 0.27309429],\n      [0.52996342, 0.50133192], [0.5976348 , 0.72837015], [0.4846008 , 0.89693948],\n      [0.68208004, 0.09615132], [0.76295886, 0.2406476 ], [0.74204944, 0.40478027],\n      [0.74241705, 0.59664122], [0.68325853, 0.90426767], [0.88884382, 0.11115617],\n      [0.90740791, 0.31405698], [0.90607266, 0.50057163], [0.90760845, 0.68688419],\n      [0.88922099, 0.88922099], [0.76367357, 0.76028947]\n  ])\n  SOTA_RADII = np.array([\n      0.08492625, 0.13325856, 0.07886036, 0.13022109, 0.08463949, 0.10518255,\n      0.11514888,\
    \ 0.11762968, 0.11207708, 0.10679013, 0.10346722, 0.10060036,\n      0.13701043, 0.09989835, 0.10306051, 0.09615132, 0.06944019, 0.09601897,\n      0.09584232, 0.09573232, 0.11115617, 0.09259208, 0.09392733, 0.09239154,\n      0.110779  , 0.06918067\n  ])\n\n  def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n  def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n  def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n      for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n           \
    \   for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                  rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      jitter_amplitudes = [1e-4, 5e-4, 1e-3, 2e-3, 3e-3, 4e-3, 5e-3]\n      restarts_per_amplitude = 5\n      \n      best_score = -1\n      best_packing = (None, None)\n      \n      bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n      constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n      for amp in jitter_amplitudes:\n          for i in range(restarts_per_amplitude):\n              seed = int(amp * 1e6) + i\n              np.random.seed(seed)\n              \n              jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=SOTA_CENTERS.shape)\n              perturbed_centers =\
    \ np.clip(SOTA_CENTERS + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n              initial_z = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, SOTA_RADII)\n              \n              res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n              \n              if res.success and -res.fun > best_score:\n                  best_score = -res.fun\n                  c, r = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                  best_packing = (c, r)\n\n      if best_packing[0] is None:\n          return _ensure_validity(SOTA_CENTERS, SOTA_RADII)\n\n      final_centers, final_radii = _ensure_validity(best_packing[0], best_packing[1])\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
