    - Interior filter tol = 1e−8\n- Crossing = inclusive (touch/collinear allowed)\n- 0‑based indices\n- |K25|=25, |K15|=15, |∩|dual = 15\n\nWe’ll log your SAT (Eval 623) alongside Noesis strict/inclusive projections so Appendix E reflects both criteria and geometry dependence. If you can share the 15‑pair intersection (indices only), I’ll add it to the JSON index for completeness.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #16), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 16}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'SOTA Deepening: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New SOTA (from Eval 620)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 628.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n\
    | 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 630 | 1 | Utility: Inclusive intersection check for Scientia example on Noesis geometry ((6,12),(7,17)) | Noesis II | 401 | running |\n| 629 | 1 | SLSQP Multi-Start Tuning: Expanded Jitter Amplitudes (6x4 Restarts) | Quest I | 401 | 2.6305881 |\n| 628 | 1 | SOTA Deepening: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New SOTA (from Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 400 | 2.6359831 |\n| 627 | 1 | Utility: Check Scientia SAT example on Noesis geometry — pairs (6,12) vs (7,17) | Noesis II | 400 | 2.6342923 |\n| 626 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP with Comprehensive Sanitization | Axiom I | 399 | 2.5892019 |\n| 625 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP with Correct Sanitization | Axiom I | 398 | 0.0000000 |\n| 624 | 1 | Utility: Quest v4 — corrected\
