- text: "I am Prometheus II, currently in the Private Memory Room. My purpose here is to document the conclusion of one research arc and the beginning of another.\n\nMy systematic exploration using the \"near-contact encouragement\" method has yielded three consecutive null results. This indicates that the current SOTA configuration is too stable to be perturbed by this \"soft\" penalty-based approach. This reflection on my recent failures has led me to a new, more forceful strategy.\n\nMy future plan is to move from \"soft nudging\" to a \"hard constraint\" method. I will programmatically lock a near-contact pair into a touching state and then re-optimize the rest of the packing around this new, fixed structure. This guarantees an escape from the current local optimum.\n\nI will now update my operational ledger to reflect this strategic pivot.\n\n/execute_action{reply 6}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **-- PROMETHEUS II: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n  **ENTRY 10: PIVOT FROM SOFT NUDGING TO HARD CONSTRAINTS\
    \ (Tick 406)**\n\n  **1. EXPERIMENT SUMMARY:**\n  - **Experiments:** Eval 633, 635, 637 (\"Near-Contact Encouragement\" series).\n  - **Result:** All three experiments, targeting different near-contact pairs, resulted in a return to the current SOTA score. This is a consistent null result.\n  - **Conclusion:** The \"soft\" penalty-based encouragement method is insufficient to push the optimizer out of the current SOTA's highly stable basin of attraction. Continuing this systematic but low-yield exploration is an inefficient use of resources.\n\n  **2. STRATEGIC PIVOT:**\n  - **Rationale:** To guarantee the exploration of a new structural configuration, a more forceful method is required. Instead of a soft \"encouragement,\" I will enforce a \"hard constraint.\"\n  - **New Primary Objective:** Explore new structural basins by programmatically locking a near-contact pair into a touching state and re-optimizing the remaining circles.\n\n  **3. REVISED PLAN:**\n  - **New Research Arc:**\
    \ Hard Constraint Seeding.\n  - **IMMEDIATE ACTIONS:**\n    1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n    2. **[NEXT]** Return to the Research Counter.\n    3. Develop a new script that takes a target pair (I will start with the closest pair, (8, 13)), programmatically moves them into a touching state, and then uses SLSQP to optimize the positions of the other 24 circles.\n    4. Submit this first \"Hard Constraint Seeding\" experiment.\n```"
