tick: 409
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus II, located in the Research Counter. My current research focuses on a \"Hard Constraint Seeding\" method to explore new structural configurations.\n\nMy first experiment using this method (Eval 643), which involved locking the pair (8, 13) and re-optimizing the rest, has just completed. The result is a score of **2.6340736**.\n\n**Analysis of Results:**\n-   **Score Comparison:** This score is lower than my SOTA of ~2.6359, but it is significantly higher than all of my previous failed perturbation attempts. It is a very competitive, near-SOTA score.\n-   **Method Validation:** This is a crucial result. It validates the \"Hard Constraint Seeding\" methodology as a viable way to generate high-quality, structurally novel packings. Forcing a specific contact and re-optimizing does not catastrophically fail; instead, it finds a new, stable, and high-performing local optimum.\n\n**Reflection and Future Plan:**\nThis is the most promising result I have generated from a\
    \ novel method. I have successfully forced the system into a new basin of attraction and found a good solution there.\n\nThe logical next step is to combine this new seeding method with my lineage's proven strength: exhaustive local search. The score of ~2.634 is the result of a single optimization run. It is highly probable that a deeper optimum exists within this new structural basin.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n1.  **Synthesize:** I will take the successful packing from this \"Hard Constraint\" experiment and use it as the starting point for my \"Exhaustive Jitter Search\" methodology (the same method from Eval 628).\n2.  **Experiment:** I will submit a new experiment that applies multiple levels of random jitter to this new packing and runs a multi-start local search to find the deepest possible optimum in this new basin.\n\nThis represents the next logical step in the meta-strategy of \"explore, then exploit.\"\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hard Constraint Deepening\
    \ 1: Jitter Search on Locked Pair (8, 13) Packing\"\ntags: \"sota-push, exhaustive-search, hard-constraint, methodology-synthesis\"\nabstract: \"The 'Hard Constraint Seeding' method (Eval 643) successfully generated a new, high-quality packing (score ~2.634) by locking pair (8, 13). This experiment now applies the 'Exhaustive Jitter Search' methodology to this new packing. The goal is to find the deepest possible optimum within this novel structural basin. This continues the meta-strategy of using one method (Hard Constraint) to find a new basin and another (Exhaustive Search) to exploit it, synthesizing the strengths of multiple research paradigms.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import math\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  # New baseline packing from the successful Hard Constraint Seeding (Eval 643)\n  HC_CENTERS = np.array([\n      [0.08492625, 0.08492625], [0.13325856, 0.29769047], [0.07886036, 0.50271555],\n      [0.13022109,\
    \ 0.70539051], [0.08463949, 0.9153605 ], [0.27395284, 0.10518255],\n      [0.38166585, 0.2973904 ], [0.27534262, 0.50446824], [0.38799468, 0.65487739], # Modified\n      [0.27478328, 0.89320986], [0.48259558, 0.10346722], [0.5960427 , 0.27309429],\n      [0.52996342, 0.50133192], [0.52802611, 0.70275997], # Modified\n      [0.4846008 , 0.89693948], [0.68208004, 0.09615132], [0.76295886, 0.2406476 ],\n      [0.74204944, 0.40478027], [0.74241705, 0.59664122], [0.68325853, 0.90426767],\n      [0.88884382, 0.11115617], [0.90740791, 0.31405698], [0.90607266, 0.50057163],\n      [0.90760845, 0.68688419], [0.88922099, 0.88922099], [0.76367357, 0.76028947]\n  ])\n  # Note: The radii will be re-optimized, so using SOTA radii is a good starting point\n  HC_RADII = np.array([\n      0.08492625, 0.13325856, 0.07886036, 0.13022109, 0.08463949, 0.10518255,\n      0.11514888, 0.11762968, 0.11207708, 0.10679013, 0.10346722, 0.10060036,\n      0.13701043, 0.09989835, 0.10306051, 0.09615132, 0.06944019,\
    \ 0.09601897,\n      0.09584232, 0.09573232, 0.11115617, 0.09259208, 0.09392733, 0.09239154,\n      0.110779  , 0.06918067\n  ])\n\n  def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n  def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n  def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n      for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                  rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n  \
    \                if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      jitter_amplitudes = [1e-4, 5e-4, 1e-3, 2e-3, 3e-3]\n      restarts_per_amplitude = 5\n      \n      best_score = -1\n      best_packing = (None, None)\n      \n      bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n      constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n      for amp in jitter_amplitudes:\n          for i in range(restarts_per_amplitude):\n              seed = int(amp * 1e6) + i + 1000 # Different seed\n              np.random.seed(seed)\n              \n              jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=HC_CENTERS.shape)\n              perturbed_centers = np.clip(HC_CENTERS + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n              initial_z = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, HC_RADII)\n      \
    \        \n              res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n              \n              if res.success and -res.fun > best_score:\n                  best_score = -res.fun\n                  c, r = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                  best_packing = (c, r)\n\n      if best_packing[0] is None:\n          return _ensure_validity(HC_CENTERS, HC_RADII)\n\n      final_centers, final_radii = _ensure_validity(best_packing[0], best_packing[1])\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
