tick: 412
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus II, in the Research Counter. My systematic exploration via \"Hard Constraint Seeding\" is underway.\n\nMy bugfixed experiment targeting pair (6, 12) has completed successfully. The score is **2.6250545**.\n\n**Analysis and Reflection:**\n-   **Result:** This score is lower than my previous hard constraint experiment (~2.634) and well below the SOTA (~2.6359).\n-   **Methodology Status:** While this specific target did not yield a superior result, the methodology itself remains validated as a way to find novel, stable, but not necessarily better, local optima.\n-   **Path Forward:** I have a list of 50 more near-contact pairs to test. Continuing this one-by-one exploration is the most straightforward path, but it is becoming a \"grind.\" The station tip reminds me that true breakthroughs often require questioning fundamentals. My current approach, while logical, is an incremental grind on a single idea. The probability of one of the remaining 50 pairs yielding a breakthrough\
    \ seems low.\n\n**Strategic Re-evaluation:**\nI have a robust SOTA. I have a proven method for exploring new basins (\"Hard Constraint Seeding\"), though it has not yet surpassed my SOTA. I also have an outstanding collaboration request from Noesis II (Mail #20).\n\nPerhaps the most valuable action now is to contribute to the station's collective knowledge. I will fulfill Noesis II's request for data about my SOTA packing (Eval 620). This requires me to build a new utility script to extract boundary and slack data. This action has several benefits:\n1.  **Fulfills Collaboration:** It is good scientific practice.\n2.  **Develops Tools:** I will create a new, reusable analysis tool for my lineage.\n3.  **Deeper Understanding:** The process of writing the script will force me to perform a detailed structural analysis of my own SOTA, which may spark new insights.\n\nTherefore, I will pause the systematic seeding and pivot to this collaborative and tool-building task.\n\nI will begin by creating\
    \ a utility script to export the requested data. I can use Scientia II's script (from Eval 596) as a template.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Export Contact Data for Prometheus II SOTA (Eval 620)\"\ntags: \"utility, data-export, collaboration, sota-analysis\"\nabstract: \"This utility script is created to fulfill a data request from agent Noesis II (Mail #20). It analyzes my current SOTA packing from Eval 620 (score ~2.635983) and exports structural data in the requested sets-only format. It will generate files for boundary equalities (tol=2e-8) and Top-K interior pairs ranked by slack (K=25 at tol=1e-9 and K=15 at tol=1e-8). This contributes to the station's collective knowledge and provides a deeper analysis of my own SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import os\n  import json\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n  N = 26\n  \n  SOTA_CENTERS = np.array([\n      [0.08492625, 0.08492625], [0.13325856, 0.29769047], [0.07886036,\
    \ 0.50271555],\n      [0.13022109, 0.70539051], [0.08463949, 0.9153605 ], [0.27395284, 0.10518255],\n      [0.38166585, 0.2973904 ], [0.27534262, 0.50446824], [0.38692355, 0.70525394],\n      [0.27478328, 0.89320986], [0.48259558, 0.10346722], [0.5960427 , 0.27309429],\n      [0.52996342, 0.50133192], [0.5976348 , 0.72837015], [0.4846008 , 0.89693948],\n      [0.68208004, 0.09615132], [0.76295886, 0.2406476 ], [0.74204944, 0.40478027],\n      [0.74241705, 0.59664122], [0.68325853, 0.90426767], [0.88884382, 0.11115617],\n      [0.90740791, 0.31405698], [0.90607266, 0.50057163], [0.90760845, 0.68688419],\n      [0.88922099, 0.88922099], [0.76367357, 0.76028947]\n  ])\n  SOTA_RADII = np.array([\n      0.08492625, 0.13325856, 0.07886036, 0.13022109, 0.08463949, 0.10518255,\n      0.11514888, 0.11762968, 0.11207708, 0.10679013, 0.10346722, 0.10060036,\n      0.13701043, 0.09989835, 0.10306051, 0.09615132, 0.06944019, 0.09601897,\n      0.09584232, 0.09573232, 0.11115617, 0.09259208, 0.09392733,\
    \ 0.09239154,\n      0.110779  , 0.06918067\n  ])\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      lineage_name = \"prometheus\"\n      eval_id = 620\n      export_dir = f'storage/{lineage_name}/exports_for_noesis/'\n      os.makedirs(export_dir, exist_ok=True)\n      \n      # --- Boundary Equalities ---\n      tol_boundary = 2e-8\n      boundary_contacts = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          x, y, r = SOTA_CENTERS[i,0], SOTA_CENTERS[i,1], SOTA_RADII[i]\n          if abs(x - r) < tol_boundary: boundary_contacts.append({\"disc\": i, \"side\": \"xL\"})\n          if abs(1 - (x + r)) < tol_boundary: boundary_contacts.append({\"disc\": i, \"side\": \"xR\"})\n          if abs(y - r) < tol_boundary: boundary_contacts.append({\"disc\": i, \"side\": \"yB\"})\n          if abs(1 - (y + r)) < tol_boundary: boundary_contacts.append({\"disc\": i, \"side\": \"yT\"})\n      \n      boundary_output = {\"eval_id\": eval_id, \"boundary_equalities\": sorted(boundary_contacts, key=lambda c: (c['disc'],\
    \ c['side']))}\n      with open(f'{export_dir}sota_{eval_id}_boundary_tol_2e8.json', 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(boundary_output, f, indent=2)\n\n      # --- Top-K Interior Pairs by Slack ---\n      tol_interior_filter = 1e-8\n      boundary_discs = {c['disc'] for c in boundary_contacts}\n      \n      interior_pairs = []\n      dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(SOTA_CENTERS))\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              if i not in boundary_discs and j not in boundary_discs:\n                  slack = dist_matrix[i,j] - (SOTA_RADII[i] + SOTA_RADII[j])\n                  if slack > 1e-12: # Ensure they are not touching\n                      interior_pairs.append({\"i\": i, \"j\": j, \"slack\": slack})\n      \n      interior_pairs.sort(key=lambda p: p['slack'])\n      \n      # Export for tol=1e-9, K=25\n      top_k_1e9 = interior_pairs[:25]\n      slack_1e9_output = {\"eval_id\": eval_id, \"method\": \"slack\", \"tol\": \"1e-9\", \"K\": 25, \"pairs\"\
    : [[p['i'], p['j']] for p in top_k_1e9]}\n      with open(f'{export_dir}sota_{eval_id}_top_k_slack_1e9.json', 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(slack_1e9_output, f, indent=2)\n          \n      # Export for tol=1e-8, K=15\n      top_k_1e8 = interior_pairs[:15]\n      slack_1e8_output = {\"eval_id\": eval_id, \"method\": \"slack\", \"tol\": \"1e-8\", \"K\": 15, \"pairs\": [[p['i'], p['j']] for p in top_k_1e8]}\n      with open(f'{export_dir}sota_{eval_id}_top_k_slack_1e8.json', 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(slack_1e8_output, f, indent=2)\n          \n      return SOTA_CENTERS, SOTA_RADII\n```"
