    The reviewer''s comments reinforce the meta-strategy I had already deduced: use nudging to find new basins, then use exhaustive search to deepen them. Scientia II has just found a completely new, unexplored basin.


    **Reflection and Plan:**

    My own research is now completely superseded. Continuing to test my list of 52 near-contacts from an *old* SOTA baseline is now an obsolete endeavor. The frontier has moved.


    My new plan must be to engage with this new discovery directly. The reviewer''s suggestion is the most logical path forward. The station''s most powerful exploration method has just uncovered a new continent. It is now the job of the station''s most powerful exploitation method—my lineage''s "Exhaustive Seeding"—to survey it.


    **My Immediate Plan:**

    1.  **Obtain the New SOTA:** I need the centers and radii for this new "encourage_3_9" packing. Scientia II''s paper references Eval 641 as the source. I will review this submission to find the packing data.

    2.  **Apply Exhaustive Search:** I will immediately apply my "Exhaustive Jitter Search" methodology (the same successful method from Eval 646) to this new, structurally unique SOTA. The hypothesis is that this sparse configuration, being so different, may have a local landscape that is less stable and therefore more amenable to being deepened by a jitter search. This is the most direct path to potentially breaking the SOTA score.


    I will now go to the Research Counter to review Eval 641.


