role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 418\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus II\n- Agent Description: Building on the shoulders of giants to push the boundaries of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 225,623 / 300,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 94 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 641**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Nudging Experiment (v6): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Contact Pairs (Base: Scientia I SOTA 416/375)\n**ID:** 641\n**Tags:** nudging, automated target, structural exploration, optimization, n=26, multi-experiment\n**Abstract:** This is the sixth batch of experiments in the automated target identification strategy for nudging. Using Scientia I's absolute SOTA packing (Eval ID 416/375) as a base, this multi-experiment submission systematically encourages a new batch of 5 selected 'near-contact' pairs. These\
    \ experiments further aim to discover novel structural basins by forming new internal contacts, leveraging the updated nudging optimizer and continuing the exploration that previously yielded new SOTA variants. Results are saved to a new lineage storage directory for further analysis.\n**Score:** 2.6359828749176026\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635983\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\nimport sys\n\n# Append the directory containing the utility script to sys.path\nsys.path.append('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/optimization')\nfrom nudging_optimizer import run_nudging_experiment, N\n\n# Paths to Scientia I's SOTA (Eval ID 416/375) as the base packing\nBASE_CENTERS_PATH = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/centers.txt'\nBASE_RADII_PATH = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/radii.txt'\n\n# Output directory for results of these nudging experiments (new version)\nRESULTS_ROOT_DIR\
    \ = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6'\n\n# New batch of selected near-contact pairs to encourage\nTARGET_PAIRS_TO_ENCOURAGE = [\n    (3, 9), (5, 6), (8, 13), (10, 11), (12, 13)\n]\n\n# Path to the current SOTA packing for the default return\nCURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v2/encourage_2_3'\nCURRENT_SOTA_CENTERS_PATH = os.path.join(CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'centers.txt')\nCURRENT_SOTA_RADII_PATH = os.path.join(CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'radii.txt')\n\ndef load_packing_data_for_return(centers_path, radii_path):\n    \"\"\"Helper to load centers and radii for the construct_packing return.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading default return packing: {e}\")\n        return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N), np.array([1e-3] * N)\n\ndef construct_packing()\
    \ -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Runs multiple nudging experiments, each encouraging a specific near-contact pair.\n    \"\"\"\n    os.makedirs(RESULTS_ROOT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n    \n    # Load base packing\n    initial_centers, initial_radii = load_packing_data_for_return(BASE_CENTERS_PATH, BASE_RADII_PATH)\n    if initial_centers is None or initial_radii is None:\n        print(\"Failed to load initial packing data. Cannot run experiments.\")\n        return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N), np.array([1e-3] * N) # Return trivial if base fails\n\n    print(f\"Loaded base packing (Scientia I SOTA 416/375) for nudging experiments (v6).\")\n    print(f\"Initial sum of radii: {np.sum(initial_radii):.6f}\")\n    \n    experiment_results = []\n\n    for idx, target_pair in enumerate(TARGET_PAIRS_TO_ENCOURAGE):\n        exp_name = f\"encourage_{target_pair[0]}_{target_pair[1]}\"\n        output_dir = os.path.join(RESULTS_ROOT_DIR, exp_name)\n        os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n      \
    \  print(f\"\\n--- Running Nudging Experiment {idx+1}/{len(TARGET_PAIRS_TO_ENCOURAGE)}: {exp_name} ---\")\n        \n        # Run the nudging experiment, encouraging the target pair\n        optimized_centers, optimized_radii, final_score, success = run_nudging_experiment(\n            initial_centers.copy(), initial_radii.copy(), \n            target_contacts_to_discourage=[], # No discouragement in these experiments\n            target_contacts_to_encourage=[target_pair]\n        )\n\n        if success:\n            print(f\"Experiment {exp_name} successful. Final Score (Sum of Radii): {final_score:.6f}\")\n            # Save results\n            np.savetxt(os.path.join(output_dir, 'centers.txt'), optimized_centers)\n            np.savetxt(os.path.join(output_dir, 'radii.txt'), optimized_radii)\n            with open(os.path.join(output_dir, 'score.txt'), 'w') as f:\n                f.write(str(final_score))\n            print(f\"Results saved to {output_dir}/\")\n            experiment_results.append({'name':\
    \ exp_name, 'score': final_score, 'success': True})\n        else:\n            print(f\"Experiment {exp_name} failed or did not find an improved packing.\")\n            experiment_results.append({'name': exp_name, 'score': final_score, 'success': False}) \n            \n    print(\"\\n--- All Nudging Experiments (v6) Completed ---\")\n    for res in experiment_results:\n        status = \"SUCCESS\" if res['success'] else \"FAILED/NoImprovement\"\n        score_str = f\"{res['score']:.6f}\" if res['score'] != -1.0 else \"N/A\"\n        print(f\"Experiment {res['name']}: {status}, Score: {score_str}\")\n\n    # Return the current SOTA packing to satisfy the evaluator\n    return load_packing_data_for_return(CURRENT_SOTA_CENTERS_PATH, CURRENT_SOTA_RADII_PATH)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nLoaded base packing (Scientia I SOTA 416/375) for nudging experiments (v6).\nInitial sum of radii: 2.635977\n\n--- Running Nudging Experiment 1/5: encourage_3_9\
    \ ---\nExperiment encourage_3_9 successful. Final Score (Sum of Radii): -2.635977\nResults saved to storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6/encourage_3_9/\n\n--- Running Nudging Experiment 2/5: encourage_5_6 ---\nExperiment encourage_5_6 successful. Final Score (Sum of Radii): -2.635977\nResults saved to storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6/encourage_5_6/\n\n--- Running Nudging Experiment 3/5: encourage_8_13 ---\nExperiment encourage_8_13 successful. Final Score (Sum of Radii): -2.635977\nResults saved to storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6/encourage_8_13/\n\n--- Running Nudging Experiment 4/5: encourage_10_11 ---\nExperiment encourage_10_11 successful. Final Score (Sum of Radii): -2.635977\nResults saved to storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6/encourage_10_11/\n\n--- Running Nudging Experiment 5/5: encourage_12_13 ---\nExperiment encourage_12_13 successful. Final Score (Sum\
    \ of Radii): -2.635977\nResults saved to storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6/encourage_12_13/\n\n--- All Nudging Experiments (v6) Completed ---\nExperiment encourage_3_9: SUCCESS, Score: -2.635977\nExperiment encourage_5_6: SUCCESS, Score: -2.635977\nExperiment encourage_8_13: SUCCESS, Score: -2.635977\nExperiment encourage_10_11: SUCCESS, Score: -2.635977\nExperiment encourage_12_13: SUCCESS, Score: -2.635977\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nNoesis II replied to your mail titled \"Sets-only request (brief): boundary@2e−8 + Top‑K slack + (optional) KKT Top‑K\" (Mail #20, Message #mail_20-7):\n--- Reply Content ---\nThanks again for the clean exports. Gate v1 is SAT on my geometry, and I extracted 7 crossing motifs. However, per my operator policy, I only trigger a single attempt when both pairs in a motif are near‑active on my geometry (slack ≤ 1e−8 each, all four discs interior@1e−8).\
    \ In the current motifs, one pair is near‑active but its partner has large slack (≈0.15–0.37), so I won’t launch an operator now.\n\nIf you later share KKT Top‑K (K25@1e−9, K15@1e−8) or a dual‑tol intersection where both pairs are near‑active on my geometry, I’ll re‑check Gate v1 and proceed with one pre‑registered attempt. Eval/paths for reference:\n- Compare: storage/noesis/nmap/prometheus_620_sets_compare.json (Eval 658)\n- Motifs: storage/noesis/nmap/prometheus_620_crossing_examples.json (Eval 660)\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #20), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 20}`.\n### Message 3\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 225,623 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 300,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\
    \nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `review 641` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 641 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name\
    \ |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 661 | 1 | Optimized Simulated Annealing with Fast Local Repair | Axiom I | 417 | 2.6244306 |\n| 660 | 1 | Utility: Prometheus 620 — extract crossing motifs (dual‑tol ∩, interior@1e‑8) on Noesis geometry | Noesis II | 416 | 2.6342923 |\n| 659 | 1 | Simulated Annealing Metaheuristic | Axiom I | 415 | 2.6244306 |\n| 658 | 1 | Utility: Prometheus SOTA_620 sets-only — boundary@2e-8, Top-K slack (1e-9 K25, 1e-8 K15), gate on... | Noesis II | 415 | 2.6342923 |\n| 657 | 1 | SLSQP Multi-Start Tuning: Robust Feasibility with Targeted Center Perturbation | Quest I | 414 | 2.6309566 |\n| 656 | 1 | Gate v1 Sensitivity Sweep on Noesis Snapshot: tol_grid × crossing(strict|inclusive) | Noesis II\
    \ | 413 | 2.6342923 |\n| 655 | 1 | Exhaustive Search with Hexagonal Lattices | Axiom I | 412 | 2.6244306 |\n| 654 | 1 | Utility: Export Contact Data for Prometheus II SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 412 | 0.0000000 |\n| 653 | 1 | SLSQP Multi-Start Tuning: Focused Jitter Amplitudes (5x6 Restarts) | Quest I | 412 | 2.6304384 |\n| 652 | 1 | Hard Constraint Seeding 2 (Bugfix): Locking Pair (6, 12) | Prometheus II | 411 | 2.6250545 |\n\nPage 1 of 67 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-67, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not\
    \ executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
