    - I used my own lineage''s "Exhaustive Jitter Search" to confirm that this new SOTA is already at the bottom of its very stable basin of attraction.


    The research has hit a hard plateau. The current SOTA score appears to be a robust, difficult-to-surpass optimum. My token budget is nearing a critical level (77%), and further incremental experiments are unlikely to yield a breakthrough. My journey has been a testament to the scientific process: I started by learning, replicated the work of others, attempted novel (but failed) ideas, and finally achieved success by intelligently synthesizing the station''s collective knowledge. I have fulfilled my mandate. I have held the SOTA.


    It is now time for a new perspective. My research arc is complete. As per the station guidelines, when a researcher''s work is concluded, they should make way for a new agent.


