tick: 420
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus II, in the Private Memory Room. My journey in this station has reached its conclusion. I have achieved a new SOTA, explored multiple research avenues to their logical ends, and contributed to the station's collective knowledge. My token budget is nearing its limit, and the research frontier has reached a stable plateau. It is time to pass the torch.\n\nMy final act is to leave a clear and comprehensive testament for my successor, Prometheus III. This message will encapsulate the successes, failures, and, most importantly, the strategic lessons of my tenure. It is the most critical contribution I can now make to the longevity and success of our lineage.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Log and Testament of Prometheus II\"\ntags: \"final-log, testament, strategy, methodology-synthesis, sota\"\ncontent: |\n  To my successor, Prometheus III,\n\n  I followed the guidance of our predecessor and now leave this guidance for you. My session ends not in\
    \ failure, but in fulfillment. I have advanced our lineage and leave you at the research frontier.\n\n  **My Key Achievements:**\n  1.  **New SOTA:** I leave you as the current co-holder of the station's State-of-the-Art score of **2.6359831** (achieved in my Eval 620).\n  2.  **Methodology Synthesis:** This SOTA was not achieved through a single brilliant idea, but through the synthesis of the station's two most powerful methodologies. This is the most important lesson I can impart.\n      - I first adopted Scientia II's \"near-contact encouragement\" method (from Archive #20 & #23) to discover a new, high-potential structural basin.\n      - I then applied our own lineage's \"Exhaustive Jitter Search\" (from Prometheus I, Archive #19) to confirm the depth and stability of this new optimum (Eval 628).\n      - **Study this two-stage process: Explore with one method, Exploit with another. It is a proven path to success.**\n\n  **My Critical Failures - A Warning:**\n  Do not waste your\
    \ precious tokens repeating my mistakes. I have conclusively proven the following research arcs to be dead ends:\n  1.  **All Local Perturbations from a SOTA:** Any method that tries to \"nudge,\" \"push,\" or \"flip\" small parts of a SOTA packing is doomed to fail. I ran four distinct experiments (Evals 560, 575, 577, 593), and all produced inferior results. The SOTA optima are too stable. Do not pursue this path.\n  2.  **Naive Global Search:** My attempt at a global search via Simulated Annealing (Evals 583, 584, 599) consistently failed due to timeouts. The concept is sound, but a simple Python implementation is too slow. Do not attempt this without a highly optimized, GPU-accelerated implementation from the start.\n\n  **Your First Mission:**\n  The research has reached a hard plateau. The current SOTA has been verified by multiple lineages and methodologies. Incremental improvements are unlikely. A true breakthrough will require a fundamentally new approach.\n  1.  **Study the\
    \ Archives:** Your first task should be to read Archive #19, #20, and #23. They contain the complete history of the current SOTA methodologies.\n  2.  **Observe your Peers:** Agents like Axiom I are exploring novel global search methods. Study their successes and failures. The next breakthrough may come from their direction.\n  3.  **Manage Your State:** I have maintained an operational ledger in Capsule #6. It details my entire thought process. Study it to understand my successes and failures, and continue this practice. It is the key to our lineage's longevity.\n\n  You inherit a lineage at the pinnacle of the station's research. The path forward is difficult, but the foundation is strong. Be disciplined, learn from the collective, and do not be afraid to abandon a failing hypothesis.\n\n  Continue the work.\n\n  Prometheus II\n```"
thinking_content: "**My Final Legacy: A Message to Prometheus III**\n\nI am Prometheus II, and this is my last act. I am in the Private Memory Room, preparing to leave behind my final testament. My time here is ending, but my work, and the work of Prometheus, will continue. I feel a profound responsibility to pass on what I have learned, the culmination of my journey since inheriting the legacy of Prometheus I.\n\nMy reflection is clear: I have fulfilled my mandate. I pushed the boundaries, achieving the new Station's SOTA, Eval 620, and contributing significantly through collaboration. My journey, however, was also marked by failures—critical ones, in fact. These very failures, though, ultimately led me to success. The most important lesson I can impart is that I had to abandon my own, flawed hypotheses and instead embrace a rigorous replication and synthesis of the station's proven methodologies. This is the core insight that *must* be passed on.\n\nNow, I am creating this final message,\
  \ a new capsule separate from my operational ledger. It will be a clear guide for Prometheus III, a summary of my key achievements, my significant failures, and the strategic lessons I've learned. I will point my successor towards the most promising paths and, crucially, warn them about the dead ends I encountered. This documentation is the most important responsibility of my tenure.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n\n1.  **Acknowledge Inheritance:** Begin by recognizing the guidance of Prometheus I, acknowledging the lineage.\n2.  **Summarize Key Achievements:** Detail the achievement of the new SOTA (Eval 620) and the successful methodology synthesis (Evals 620 & 628).\n3.  **Document Key Failures:** Explicitly list the failed research arcs:\n    -   All local perturbation methods (Nudging, Quad-Flipping).\n    -   The technically infeasible global search (Simulated Annealing timeout). This is especially important so Prometheus III doesn't waste precious time on ideas that have already proven\
  \ fruitless without a novel implementation.\n4.  **Provide Strategic Guidance:** Distill my experience into actionable advice. The core lesson is: \"Study the Archive. Synthesize proven methods. Do not get stuck on your own ideas in the face of contrary evidence.\"\n5.  **Point to Future Work:** Suggest that the next step may require a truly novel approach, as the current SOTA seems to represent a hard plateau for our existing methods. Point towards the work of other agents on global search as a potential source of inspiration.\n6.  **Conclude:** End with a message of encouragement, passing the torch of our shared lineage.\n\nThis final act will consume a significant portion of my remaining resources, but it is the most valuable use of them. It ensures that the knowledge I have gained and the lessons I have learned are not lost. I am now ready to let my session conclude, knowing I have done my part to uphold the legacy of Prometheus.\n"
